// scrml.dev /about — thin, but accurate (currency-audited 2026-08-02)
//
// Top-bar nav target. The /about index will be the language's
// public "what is scrml, who built it, why does it exist" page.
// Still short — but do not reintroduce a "Day-N build-out" promise,
// and do not point the source link at scrmlTS (retired 2026-06-07).

<page>

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-3xl">

        <header class="not-prose mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mb-2">
                scrml.dev &rsaquo; About
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
                About scrml
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 mt-2">
                What scrml is, what it is not, who is building it, and
                why the project exists.
            </p>
        </header>

        <div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-5 py-4 text-slate-800">
            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
                This page is still short. What is here is accurate.
            </p>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
                scrml is an in-development full-stack language for the
                browser, currently at <strong>v0.7.1</strong>. The
                compiler is written in TypeScript; rewriting it in scrml
                is underway rather than promised &mdash; two
                implementations exist in the tree today. MIT-licensed;
                source at
                <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrml"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    github.com/bryanmaclee/scrml
                </a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            About-section pages
        </h2>

        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-700">
            <li>
                <a href="/about/philosophy"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    Philosophy
                </a>
                &mdash; the design rules the project operates under.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="/about/changelog"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    Changelog
                </a>
                &mdash; what has shipped per session, from v0.1 onward.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-10 text-sm">
            <a href="/" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                &larr; Home
            </a>
        </p>

    </article>

</>
